    {
      "text": "Then 10 minutes later, I'm standing over an open suitcase, holding a third pair of jeans, thinking, \"Yeah, but what if I need options?\" I fold things, unfold them, roll them, refold them, and the suitcase still never closes the same way twice. And there's always that one thing I forget. It doesn't matter how careful I am. Toothbrush, socks, phone charger, something always gets left behind every single time. The funny part is, I pack like I'm going on an expedition, not a weekend trip. Extra shoes, a jacket just in case, even snacks like I might get stranded somewhere with no civilization. And when it's finally time to go, I zip it up, sit on the suitcase for good measure, and hope I actually remember the important stuff. Packing for a trip always starts with excitement and ends with me double checking everything twice and still wondering what I forgot.",
